[WORK]
UID: WORK-SPLIT-MEGA-NODES
TITLE: Three work items grew into several topics each
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
WORK-ANNOTATION-NODES, WORK-CODE-LINKAGE-EXTRACTORS and WORK-GRAMMAR-TAB-GROUPS
each grew by appending verbatim paragraphs to NOTES across several sessions, so
each now covers several topics at once. That is the anti-pattern
WORK-ONE-NODE-ONE-TOPIC rules against: node count is supposed to carry
complexity. Cheapest fix: split each into one node per topic, keeping the
original UID for whichever topic is the trunk.
<<<
